This repository operates under a strict Dual-Licensing Model, separating open-source community rights from commercial exemptions. The SPDX composite identifier `(CERN-OHL-S-2.0 AND AGPL-3.0-or-later)` at the repository root does NOT apply uniformly to all files. Instead, it describes a composite model where specific artifact classes are governed by specific licenses, as defined below:

----------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SCOPE & ARTIFACT CLASSIFICATION MAPPING
----------------------------------------------------------------------

A. HARDWARE PRODUCTION RTL & VERIFICATION SOURCE (SPDX: CERN-OHL-S-2.0)
   - Scope: Production Register-Transfer Level modules (`rtl/*.sv`), simulation testbenches
     (`tb/*.sv`), and formal verification proof harnesses (`fv/*.sv`).
   - Excluded / Unreleased: Reference PCB layouts, electrical CAD schematics, and Gerber
     manufacturing files are not published in this repository and are not covered by this release.
   - Governing Terms: Released under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Strongly Reciprocal
     Version 2.0 (CERN-OHL-S-2.0). Licence permissions, conditions, and obligations—including
     the grant of rights (§2), distribution conditions (§3), and provisions governing making
     and Conveying Products (§4) and Complete Source (§1.8)—are governed strictly by all
     applicable terms of CERN-OHL-S-2.0. This summary notice does not alter, replace, or narrow
     any terms of the official licence.

B. VERIFICATION SCRIPTS & REPOSITORY TOOLING
   - Script Tooling: The verification script `scripts/verify_gate_b_rev28d.ps1` currently carries
     an internal SPDX-License-Identifier for CERN-OHL-S-2.0 as repository tooling. CI workflow
     configurations (`.github/workflows/*.yml`) provide automation configuration.
   - Software Boundary: Embedded controller software, companion firmware, and NPU driver hooks
     are not included in this hardware repository. If companion software packages are released
     in the future, they will be distributed in separate repositories under designated software licenses.

C. NORMATIVE METHODOLOGY & SPECIFICATION DOCUMENTS
   - Scope: Architectural specifications, conformance test specifications, and evidence
     matrices (`zero-cloud-*.md`).
   - Copyright Claim & Document Notices: FreeCuli claims copyright over the textual expression
     of documentation files authored for this repository, which are governed by their respective
     individual document notices (with core specifications displaying individual CERN-OHL-S-2.0 notices).
     This copyright claim is not characterized as an independently verified legal determination.
   - Functional Implementation Boundary: Reading and evaluating the specification text is permitted
     under its applicable terms. Conforming to the functional methodology described in the
     specifications does not convey to FreeCuli intellectual property rights over an implementer's
     independently authored hardware designs.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. LICENSING PATHWAYS & COMMERCIAL EXEMPTIONS (ROUTE B)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
FreeCuli defines two licensing pathways for its covered RTL source code:

Route A (Reciprocal Open Hardware):
  Any organization or individual—commercial or non-commercial—may freely exercise licence
  rights under CERN-OHL-S-2.0, subject to all applicable terms and conditions of the official
  licence, including the grant of rights (§2), copyleft/distribution conditions (§3), and
  obligations regarding making Products, Conveyance, and Complete Source (§1.8, §4).

Route B (Elective Separate Commercial License):
  Organizations seeking to incorporate FreeCuli's reference RTL designs into closed-source
  products without releasing derivative RTL under CERN-OHL-S-2.0 may negotiate an elective,
  separate commercial license with FreeCuli.
  Scope & Limitations: Any Route B agreement is a contractually defined alternative licensing
  pathway strictly limited to source materials where FreeCuli holds licensing authority (which,
  in this repository, is grounded in the founder's factual representation ATTEST-01 over `rtl/*.sv`,
  not an independently verified chain of title) and to the express terms of that agreement.
  Route B does not provide an automatic blanket exemption for an entire multi-vendor product,
  does not license third-party IP or patents, and does not retroactively alter, revoke, or extinguish
  any rights previously acquired or obligations previously incurred under CERN-OHL-S-2.0.

Independent Implementations & Intellectual Property Boundaries:
  Independent development of hardware from functional specifications without copying
  FreeCuli's protected RTL source does not, in itself, constitute copyright infringement of
  FreeCuli's RTL source code. This statement applies strictly and exclusively to FreeCuli's
  own RTL copyright claims. It does not provide a universal liability shield: third-party patent
  validity, contractual commitments, trade secrets, and trademark designations ("FreeCuli Certified™")
  remain distinct legal inquiries governed by applicable law and specific factual circumstances.

